{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.BarInvolutionInvariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.BarInvolutionInvariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.bar_involution_invariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.bar_involution_invariance","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L223-L231","doc":"Top-level invariance bundle (the proposition's main claim). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:bar-involution-invariance","label":"prop:bar-involution-invariance","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.bar_involution_invariance_witness_scope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.bar_involution_invariance_witness_scope","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L216-L221","doc":"Witness scope tag.  The numerical bar-invariance / transpose-\npair check covers every `λ ⊢ n` for `n ∈ {0, 1, …, 9}`.  Total\npartition count tested: `1 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11 + 15 + 22 +\n30 = 97`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.normal_form_bar_invariant_conditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.normal_form_bar_invariant_conditional","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L198-L205","doc":"**Step (3)**, conditional on the upstream conjecture: every\nType-B-folded normal form is bar-invariant.  Proof body has no\n`sorry`; the only unproved input is the class instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.bar_invariant_outputs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.bar_invariant_outputs","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L194-L194","doc":"Bar-invariance is enforced by the folded operator pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L192-L192","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction","kind":"class","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L189-L196","doc":"Class-form axiomatisation of conj:symmetric-crystal-pair-production.\nThe single field encodes the conjecture content: every emitted\nnormal form is bar-invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.isPairProductionOutput","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.isPairProductionOutput","kind":"axiom","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L183-L187","doc":"A predicate isolating those normal forms emitted by the\npair-production engine (opaque; its content is the conjectural\nsymmetric-crystal pair-production engine, not a provable proposition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.barNormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.barNormalForm","kind":"axiom","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L177-L181","doc":"The bar-involution acting on a Hecke normal form (`q ↦ q⁻¹`,\ncrossings reversed). Opaque accessor; the involution is the standard Hecke\nbar-involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.HeckeNormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.HeckeNormalForm","kind":"axiom","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L172-L175","doc":"The Hecke normal form carrier (opaque; full structure in\n`hecke-normal-form.lean`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.plancherel_weight_transpose_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.plancherel_weight_transpose_eq","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L149-L162","doc":"**Step (2)**: `w_λ(q) = w_{λᵀ}(q)`.\n\nHook lengths are preserved (as multisets) under partition\ntranspose, so the product over hooks is unchanged.  The\ntransport from `List.Perm` to `List.prod` equality is the\nstandard `List.Perm.prod_eq` lemma. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.plancherel_weight_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.plancherel_weight_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L132-L147","doc":"**Step (1)**: `w_λ(q⁻¹) = w_λ(q)`.\n\nEach hook factor `[h]_q⁻¹` is bar-invariant by\n`q_integer_bar_invariant`; products and squares of bar-\ninvariants are bar-invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.plancherelWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.plancherelWeight","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L120-L130","doc":"The (unnormalised) `q`-deformed Plancherel weight of a\npartition: `w_λ(q) := (∏_{h ∈ hookLengths λ} [h]_q⁻¹)^2`.\nThe full normalisation `/ [n]_q!` is a global constant\nindependent of `λ`, so the lemmas below transfer.\n\nImplemented via `List.prod` (rather than a hand-rolled\n`foldr`) so that the transpose-invariance proof can transport\nvia `List.Perm.prod_eq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.hookLengths_transpose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.hookLengths_transpose","kind":"axiom","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L113-L118","doc":"Hook lengths are preserved by transpose (Mathlib\n`YoungDiagram.transpose_hookLengths` once available). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.partitionTranspose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.partitionTranspose","kind":"axiom","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L106-L111","doc":"The transpose involution (Dynkin fold; cf.\ncpt-orbit-closure-density.lean). Opaque accessor on the `Partition` carrier;\nthe concrete map is `YoungDiagram.transpose` once `Partition` is wired to\nMathlib's `YoungDiagram`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.hookLengths","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.hookLengths","kind":"axiom","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L103-L104","doc":"Hook-length list of a partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.Partition","kind":"axiom","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L99-L101","doc":"Hook-length sequence of a partition (carrier; full structure\nin `Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.q_integer_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.q_integer_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L66-L89","doc":"**Step (1) base lemma**: `[k]_{q^{-1}} = [k]_q` for `q > 0, q ≠ 1`.\n\nDirect calculation: under `q ↦ 1/q`,\n\n* numerator `q^k − q^{−k}` flips sign and swaps terms\n  (since `(1/q)^k = q^{−k}` and `(1/q)^{−k} = q^k`),\n* denominator `q − q⁻¹` flips sign\n  (since `(1/q)⁻¹ = q`).\n\nThe two sign flips cancel.  Closed with `field_simp; ring` after\nexpanding `(1/q)^k = (q^k)⁻¹` via `inv_pow` and the ℤ-power\n`q^{−k} = (q^k)⁻¹` via `zpow_neg_natCast`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.qInteger_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.qInteger_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L58-L64","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical balanced bracket.** This site writes the inverse\nas the `zpow` `q ^ (-(k : ℤ))`; `qIntBal` writes `q⁻¹ ^ k`. Equal, but not\ndefinitionally, so the consolidation is this equation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.qInteger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.qInteger","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L54-L56","doc":"The q-integer `[k]_q = (q^k − q^{−k}) / (q − q^{−1})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.barInvolution_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.barInvolution_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L45-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.barInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.barInvolution","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/bar-involution-invariance.lean#L42-L43","doc":"The bar involution: `q ↦ q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}